# Feature registry

Every in-scope product maintains `docs/FEATURES.md` — a living, flat list of shipped features (name + one-line description). It answers "what can this app actually do today," not "what changed" (that's git history) or "what's planned" (that's `docs/PLAN.md` / `docs/LEFTOVER_CHECKLIST.md`).

## Rule: keep it in sync automatically

Whenever a `docs/LEFTOVER_CHECKLIST.md` item is marked `[x]` (done, with proving tests per the doc-pack rule), add a one-line row to `docs/FEATURES.md` **in the same commit** — not as a separate follow-up task. If the completed item is not user-facing (pure refactor, internal tooling, config, dependency bump), skip the entry; don't pad the registry with non-features.

Same applies in reverse: when new PLAN-phase work ships a feature directly (without ever being a Leftover item), add the row when that work lands.

## Required for every in-scope product

`docs/FEATURES.md` is part of the required doc pack (see [`docs/AGENTIC_DOC_PACK.md`](../../docs/AGENTIC_DOC_PACK.md) §2). Scaffold new products from [`docs/agentic-templates/FEATURES.md`](../../docs/agentic-templates/FEATURES.md).

For existing products where `docs/FEATURES.md` doesn't exist yet, reverse-engineer it once from the current codebase (routes, modules, README, SRS FR-IDs) rather than starting blank — then keep it in sync going forward per the rule above.

## Exclusions

Same exclusions as the doc pack (see [`doc-pack-exclusions.mdc`](./doc-pack-exclusions.mdc)): `food-delivery-multivendor`, `erp-lite`.
